  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Community Recovery and Resilience Facility (CRRF) project is a crucial initiative aimed at bolstering resilience of communities in Eastern and Southern Africa severely affected by the recurring impacts of El Ni&#xf1;o Southern Oscillation (ENSO) events. This project represents the first phase of a broader recovery facility, with the current interventions serving as pilot programs that will inform and guide a larger-scale effort in subsequent phases.</narrative>
  </description>
